{
 "name": "loop_slice_corner",
 "description": "Loop Slice with Slice Selected ON, over an L-SHAPED face selection -- the gesture the chapter performs repeatedly (a band of polygons that turns a corner) and the one our only existing Slice Selected fixture cannot exercise, because its two faces are a straight run. KNOWN DIVERGENCE, measured 2026-08-16: the reference cuts ONE path that TURNS at the corner cell -- entering through one edge and leaving through a PERPENDICULAR one -- which is what its documentation means by 'respects corners as well'. vibe3d instead cuts BOTH rings clipped to the selection, so the two cuts CROSS inside the corner cell. Our vertex set is a strict superset of the reference's: the same six points plus the crossing point at the corner cell's centre and the two extra exits where each ring runs on to its own end of the L.",
 "source": "LIVE-CAPTURED from the reference editor, driven headlessly through its command line. A 3x1x3 box, the top face's 3x3 grid, an L of five cells selected by centroid predicate (the row at z=-1/3 plus the column at x=+1/3), then its loop-slice tool with the slice-selected option on and a count of one, applied through the tool-apply command. Base and result were both dumped; the reference's answer is 38 verts / 71 edges / 35 polys against a 32/60/30 base. Three different values of its current-edge attribute were captured separately and produced identical geometry, so the ring is derived from the selection, not from that attribute.",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
  "source": "live-capture",
  "reference": "ref-editor@11.2v3",
  "method": "command",
  "captured_utc": "2026-08-16",
  "harness": "tools/local/capture (task 1053)",
  "task": "1053",
  "notes": "The tool APPLIES headlessly -- set the tool, set its attributes, apply, drop it: no viewport gesture and no pointer injection, which the 0263 capture note had recorded as needing an interactive commit. So the drag-transport artifact does not apply to this measurement."
 },
